{"duration_ms":0,"id":18,"kind":"llm","model":"claude-opus-5","name":"claude-code.turn.11","provider":"anthropic","response":{"content":[{"text":"`slug('Hello, World')` now returns `'hello-world'`. All 5 tests pass.\n\nThe fix follows the ordering the docstring warns about — punctuation is stripped *before* hyphenation, so the filter never sees (and can't eat) the hyphens it just inserted:\n\n```python\ncleaned = \"\".join(\n    c for c in title.lower() if c.isalnum() or c.isspace() or c == \"-\"\n)\nreturn \"-\".join(cleaned.split())\n```\n\nTwo side effects worth knowing about:\n- Hyphens already in the title survive (`\"Well-Known Name\"` → `\"well-known-name\"`), since they're allowed through the filter.\n- `split()` collapses whitespace runs, so `\"hello,  world\"` gives one hyphen rather than two.\n\nAdded tests covering punctuation removal and hyphen preservation.","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011CevH21Qo9HUqMyL59Lc4N","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":140,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":140,"cache_read_input_tokens":18665,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"start_ms":0,"usage":{"cache_read":18665,"cache_write_1h":140,"input":2,"output":1}}
